  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The HUBZone set-aside program obligated $424M in FY2026 to date. The program produced 1,231 awards with an average award size of $344K. Obligations fell 54.0% year over year. Historical context shows earlier fiscal-year totals of $938M in FY21, $1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1B in FY24, and $920M in FY25. The Department of Defense led buying with $146M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $75.3M and the Department of Labor with $51.4M. Other significant buyers include the Department of Transportation ($30.6M), the Department of Health and Human Services ($26.1M), and the Department of State ($14.9M). Other Computer Related Services is the largest industry by obligations at $116M, with construction and training categories following. Top vendors include T&H SERVICES, LLC ($22.8M), PANAMERICA COMPUTERS, INC. ($19.2M), and ANACAPA MICRO PRODUCTS, INC. ($19.1M). All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The HUBZone set-aside program obligated $424M in FY2026 to date, a drop from prior fiscal years. Obligations fell 54.0% year over year. Award activity produced 1,231 awards with an average award size of $344K, indicating fewer or smaller awards compared with the $1.1B peak in FY23. The fiscal-year series shows a decline from FY23 through FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are the HUBZone dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $146M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $75.3M and the Department of Labor with $51.4M. Other Computer Related Services leads industries with $116M, while Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Other Technical and Trade Schools each account for sizable shares at $41.9M and $41.6M respectively. Top vendors include T&H SERVICES, LLC ($22.8M) and PANAMERICA COMPUTERS, INC. ($19.2M)."
      }
    ]
  },
