    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through HUBZone set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $424M through HUBZone set-asides in FY2026 to date. The program produced 1,231 awards with an average award size of $344K, and obligations fell 54.0% year over year. Historical obligations were $938M in FY21, $1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1B in FY24, and $920M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use HUBZone set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense uses HUBZone set-asides the most, with $146M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $75.3M and the Department of Labor with $51.4M, then the Departments of Transportation, Health and Human Services, and State at $30.6M, $26.1M, and $14.9M respectively."
    },
